    "name": "Healbane",
    "compareWith": "Spirit Lifesteal",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obscure",
    "reason": "Healbane is a niche anti-heal item that players rarely buy and few would associate with 1,600 souls. Spirit Lifesteal is a core, widely recognised spirit item, so it is more likely to be named.",
    "outcome": "applied"
   },
   {
    "name": "Active Reload",
    "compareWith": "Bullet Lifesteal",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obscure",
    "reason": "Active Reload is a fairly niche weapon item. Bullet Lifesteal is a staple purchase that comes to mind more readily, so it should not sit 50 points more obvious.",
    "outcome": "rejected-by-comparison"
   },
   {
    "name": "Slowing Hex",
    "compareWith": "Mystic Slow",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obscure",
    "reason": "Slowing Hex is a rarely bought, easily forgotten item, and nothing ties it to the 1,600 price. Placing it in the top 10-point tier is unjustified. It should be nearer to the other obscure items.",
    "outcome": "rejected-by-comparison"
   },
   {
    "name": "Cold Front",
    "compareWith": "Return Fire",
    "claim": "should_be_more_obvious",
    "reason": "Cold Front is a distinctive, commonly built spirit item that experienced players know well. It is not a 30-point item next to the mid-tier items. Return Fire is more forgettable than it.",
    "outcome": "ignored-invalid"
   },
